I know @pcalcado touched on this too, so sorry to swoop in with an additional refactor suggestion.

We don't have an official style guide at Buoyant, but I tend to use the [Go Code Review Comments](https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/CodeReviewComments) guide. And this section of the guide is relevant to how this method is written:

https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/CodeReviewComments#indent-error-flow

The basic idea is to return as early as possible (like you do in the first if condition), and then continue executing the main path of the function. In most cases, this means avoiding else clauses. So now that you're returning immediately if `apiHostAndPortOverride == ""`, then you don't need to wrap the rest of the logic in this function in an else clause. It could be written like this:

```
	if apiHostAndPortOverride == "" {
		return &kubernetesApi{
			apiSchemeHostAndPort: config.Host,
			config:               config,
		}, nil
	}

	parsedURL, err := url.Parse(apiHostAndPortOverride)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, fmt.Errorf("error parsing override url: %v", err)
	}

	if parsedURL.Scheme == "" {
		apiHostAndPortOverride = fmt.Sprintf("https://%s", apiHostAndPortOverride)
	}

	return &kubernetesApi{
		apiSchemeHostAndPort: apiHostAndPortOverride,
		config:               config,
	}, nil
```

Cool, you're definitely on the right track here. I'd like to see this method written as:

```
func newPublicAPIClient() (pb.ApiClient, error) {
	if apiAddr != "" {
		return public.NewInternalClient(apiAddr)
	}

	kubeApi, err := k8s.NewK8sAPI(shell.NewUnixShell(), kubeconfigPath)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}

	return public.NewExternalClient(controlPlaneNamespace, kubeApi)
}
```

My rationale here is: we don't need to call `k8s.NewK8SAPI` if `apiAddr != ""`. So instead I'd prefer for this method to start with the CLI input strings, and only instantiate objects as needed. And if we're working with the CLI inputs (`apiAddr` and `kubeconfigPath`), then we don't need those passed in as parameters, since they're defined globally in this package.

The other change here is that we shouldn't need to pass `apiAddr` as a parameter to `k8s.NewK8sAPI`, since the apiAddr override has already been applied by the time we call that function. See my comments below for changes related to this.

But the status command is an exception to the rule, since we do actually want to know if the call to `k8s.NewK8sAPI` failed. In that case, I'd suggest rewriting this block of code as:

```
		kubeApi, err := k8s.NewK8sAPI(shell.NewUnixShell(), kubeconfigPath)
		if err != nil {
			fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "Error with Kubernetes API: %s\n", err.Error())
			return statusCheckResultWasError(os.Stdout)
		}

		var conduitApi pb.ApiClient
		if apiAddr != "" {
			conduitApi, err = public.NewInternalClient(apiAddr)
		} else {
			conduitApi, err = public.NewExternalClient(controlPlaneNamespace, kubeApi)
		}
		if err != nil {
			fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "Error with Conduit API: %s\n", err.Error())
			return statusCheckResultWasError(os.Stdout)
		}
```

