From looking at the gorilla documentation, it looks like all closes are returned as errors, even if they're expected. And we can check for expected closes using the [IsUnexpectedCloseError](https://godoc.org/github.com/gorilla/websocket#IsUnexpectedCloseError) (see example in the godoc). Based on that example, I'd write this as:

```
for {
	_, _, err := ws.ReadMessage()
	if err != nil {
		if websocket.IsUnexpectedCloseError(err, websocket.CloseNormalClosure) {
			log.Errorf("Unexpected close error: %s", err)
		}
		return
	}
}
```

