TIL that the `pod.status.containerStatuses[].image` field in the pod API response isn't guaranteed to match the `pod.spec.containers[].image` field. In my environment I have the same proxy image tagged multiple times, and as far as I can tell, the status container arbitrarily picks which image tag it uses, whereas the spec container reflects what's actually in the spec. So for instance, when I look at my injected controller pod, I see different strings for the proxy's spec container and the status container:

```
$ curl -s localhost:8001/api/v1/namespaces/linkerd/pods/controller-7b9df96664-lxm9p | jq -S . | grep 'proxy:'
        "image": "gcr.io/linkerd-io/proxy:git-05e6d58e",
        "image": "gcr.io/linkerd-io/proxy:dev-37884805-kl",
```

So I think we need to use the spec container when populating the image field in the pod struct. This should do it:

```
		proxyReady := false
