   string uuid = 1;
 
```

Granted, we don't have a lot of precedent around the organization of this file just yet. But if we're going to treat `Global` as a grab bag of configuration options, I'd be inclined to do away with the multiple config struct setup, and instead move the proxy config options into the global struct as well. But if we're going to try to separate out different types of a configuration, this would be a good opportunity to add a third, top-level `Install` struct.

At the end of the day, I don't have a strong preference, but I want to take whichever approach avoids an unmanageable mess of configuration options :)

