@adleong I've confirmed that we do need this and was able to verify with additional unit tests.  Here's the process I'm guarding against:

Install using `linkerd install --registry=install.registry` results in ConfigMap settings like:
```
data:
  proxy: {"imageName":"install.registry/proxy",...}
  install: {"flags":[{"name":"registry", "value":"install.registry"}],...}
```

Inject using `linkerd inject --registry=inject.registry` will still only inject `install.registry/proxy`.

The injected image is not overridden because the current `registryOverride()` method in `install.go` only replaces the _default_ registry, i.e. `gcr.io/linkerd-io`.  In our case, we want to have the new registry override `install.registry` which we only know by looking at the installation flags.

The `registryOverride()` method in `install.go` is fine as it is, but should not be used by `inject.go`.

