@briansmith 
> Is this a step towards segmenting what is currently called "labels" into different types of things, so that "labels" will eventually become only about telemetry reporting and not about, e.g. TLS or other non-telemetry stuff?

I believe this is already the case --- the non-telemetry stuff lives in `Metadata`, alongside the `labels`, which are used only by Tap and metrics.

@briansmith that's right.  This has already (largely) been done for transport metrics, though it's in a somewhat incremental state of refactoring. I'm hoping that we get to an end state where there's an `http` module that has _all_ of the http-specific concerns, a `transport` module that has _all_ of the transport-specific concerns, etc.

I very much want to kill off the central `labels` module (I think most of what's left there is HTTP-specific, which is next on my hit list after the transport refactor moves a little further), the `ctx` module, and any other module where we have cross-cutting concerns intermingled.

I should also point out https://github.com/linkerd/linkerd2-proxy/pull/67, which will let us start to more clearly separate the metrics-rendering concerns from caching/structural concerns.
